# Version control
.git
.gitignore

# Documentation and planning artifacts
_bmad-output/
_research/
*.md
!README.md

# Frontend directory (not needed in backend build context)
web/

# Test artifacts
tests/
coverage.out
*.test

# Build artifacts
bin/
tally-backend
tally-backend.exe
# `tally-backend.exe` alone was not enough: the tree also accumulates
# server.exe / tally-mcp.exe / kill-switch-monitor.exe from `go build` on
# Windows. Measured 2026-08-11: 55.4M + 11.1M + 8.7M = 75.2M of the build
# context. `**/` prefix because a bare `*.exe` only matches the root level.
**/*.exe

# Agent/session working directory. Measured 2026-08-11 with a probe image
# (`COPY . /ctx` + `du`): 563.3M — 86% of a 655.6M build context, for a
# backend image whose builder stage only reads internal/ cmd/ migrations/
# go.mod go.sum (~5.5M). The daemon still has to receive every byte before
# the first instruction runs; on this machine that was 101.7s of a 4m54.9s
# cold build. CI does a fresh checkout so it never sees this — which is
# exactly why it went unnoticed.
.claude/

# UAT run outputs (10.0M measured). Six files are tracked, so unlike the
# above this one does reach CI's context too.
_uat-reports/

# Secrets
.env

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
